_vs_hist":36.7,"_gate_fcf_yield":0.03203444709367079,"_gp_fcf_yield":false,"_score_fcf_yield":12.2,"_gate_int_coverage":5.7526132404181185,"_gp_int_coverage":true,"_score_int_coverage":25.0,"_gate_net_debt_ebitda":2.5465207193119626,"_gp_net_debt_ebitda":false,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":32.3,"_gate_accruals":-0.06275827853110633,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":71.9,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.08923600153190739,"_gp_rev_volatility":true,"_score_rev_volatility":88.8,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.01825854513228012,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":77.2,"_gate_piotroski":4,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":0.031097916936055153,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":15.5,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.2538276708783779,"_gp_roic_consistency":true,"_score_roic_consistency":57.7,"_gate_incr_roic":0.1636801955501545,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":71.2,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.0848613175491841,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":61.6,"_gate_pool_share":0.016107868147174687,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":46.4,"_gate_rev_durability":0.05297191579366611,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":51.5,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.13534847394906713,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":92.7,"_gate_margins":0.0016074016544365577,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":51.6,"_gate_fund_growth":0.014480679204654123,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":14.5,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.021382893701379257,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":34.9,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.004680258570775919,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":55.9,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.002280377891193398,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":96.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.0018000001,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":1.2,"_gate_insider_buying":0.986,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":98.6,"pf":[],"description_full":"Republic Services, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, offers environmental services in the United States and Canada. It is involved in the collection and processing of recyclable, solid waste, and industrial waste materials; transportation and disposal of non-hazardous and hazardous waste streams; and other environmental solutions. Its residential collection services include curbside collection of material for transport to transfer stations, landfills, recycling centers, and organics processing facilities; supply of recycling and waste containers; and renting of compactors. The company also engages in the processing and sale of old corrugated containers, old newsprint, aluminum, glass, and other materials; and provision of landfill services. It serves small-container, large-container, and residential customers. The company was incorporated in 1996 and is based in Phoenix, Arizona.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jon  Vander Ark | President, CEO & Director | Age 50 | Compensation: $3.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 42K people. Revenue per employee of $453K ranks in the above the sector median among Industrials peers, improving at 5%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $57K of free cash flow annually. CEO compensation is 8\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Republic Services, Inc. is a large-cap industrials business with a $75.2B market cap on $19.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +7% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 7% cost of capital, a 3-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $2.4B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 13 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.01\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 5.8\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 2.1% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.13303437967115125},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Significant goodwill (49% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Industrials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 8% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Insiders are net buyers (99% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Large open-market insider purchases (net $1193.0M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","22 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Is Syama's Sulphide Conversion the Make-or-Break Factor for Resolute (ASX:RSG)?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/au/stocks/gold/is-syamas-sulphide-conversion-the-make-or-break-factor-for-resolute-asxrsg","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793936520.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.687,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"If You Invested $100 In Republic Services Stock 10 Years Ago, You Would Have This Much Today","source":"benzinga.com","link":"https://www.benzinga.com/news/26/11/62992800/if-you-invested-100-republic-services-stock-10-years-ago-you-would-have-much-today","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793982625.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Waste Management vs. Republic Services: Which Pays Investors More?","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/waste-management-vs-republic-services-131741000.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793971547.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.118,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Zacks Investment Ideas feature highlights: Republic Services and Cintas","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3025305/zacks-investment-ideas-feature-highlights-republic-services-and-cintas?cid=CS-ZC-FT-press_releases-3025305","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793969580.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"What Resolute Mining Doubters Got Wrong","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/au/materi