3% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 20% and a beta of 0.42, it is more defensive than the market, though its beta has shifted (1y -0.57 vs 5y 0.36), so read it loosely.","Liquidity is deep, with about $307.4M traded a day.","In past sell-offs it fell 34% in the 2020 crash, 15% in the 2022 bear market and 54% in 2008."],"val":["The price sits above its DCF fair value of $223 (margin of safety -11%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models corroborate one another (dispersion 13%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $166 to $312 (P10-P90).","On multiples it looks expensive against Industrials peers: P/E 34.2 vs 23.3, EV/EBITDA 16.8 vs 13.3 and P/FCF 31.2 vs 22.3 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 45% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of 3.2% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 3.7% (vs the 8% bar).","The 24 covering analysts target $256 on average, 4% above the price."],"prof":["ROIC of 10% earns above the cost of capital of 7.0%, but the 3pp spread is short of the 7pp moat bar; returns have been steady (CV 0.25).","It converts 13% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 2.01x.","ROE of 18% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.9x equity multiplier).","It spends 0.2% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 2.5x net debt to EBITDA ($76.0M of cash against $13.1B of debt), above the 1.5x gate, with interest covered 5.8x.","The current ratio of 0.64 means short-term liabilities exceed current assets.","Goodwill makes up 49% of assets, a soft asset exposed to impairment."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 6.7% over 3 years, 9.6% over 5 years and 5.3% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating.","At current returns, reinvesting 14% of profits supports about 1.4% a year of fundamental growth, too little to drive meaningful growth.","Free cash flow has compounded 13.5% a year over five years.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 2%.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (1.0x, 9.9% of sales), a maintenance pace.","Its Rule of 40 score is 21, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.2%), and institutions hold 100%.","Insider trading is two-way: 72 purchases and 1 sale over the past year, net $1.2B bought.","It returns 2.1% a year to shareholders (1.2% in buybacks and 1.1% in dividends).","It has paid a dividend for 22 consecutive years, raising it 7.2% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 42,000 employees, each generates about $453K of revenue, 1.2x the Industrials median, and productivity has risen 5.4% a year.","That works out to $57K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $3.7M (8x revenue per employee)."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":57,"head":"Watch: LEAN BUY-rated, but no margin of safety; it becomes a buy below $189.","pros":["Model rating LEAN BUY (composite 47, gates 16/25)","FCF margin 12.7%","Revenue grew 9.6%/yr over 5y","Altman Z in the safe zone","Insiders net buyers ($1.2B over 12 months)"],"cons":["Trades 11% above fair value of $223","P/E 34.2x vs sector 23.3x","EV/EBITDA 16.8x vs sector 13.3x","P/FCF 31.2x vs sector 22.3x"],"flags":[],"need":["no margin of safety"],"buy_below":189.33,"vc":{"base":222.74,"base_src":"dcf","bear":166.28,"bull":312.33,"alt_median":103.24,"n_alt":3,"gap":1.1574,"dispersion":0.1252,"level":"LOW","why":["DCF is 116% above the other models' median ($103)"]},"med":{"pe":23.2692,"ev_ebitda":13.319,"pfcf":22.2778,"pb":3.0551,"roic":0.1001,"gross_margin":0.2851,"fcf_margin":0.068,"div_yield":0.0147}},"ticker":"RSG","date":"2026-11-06"}